{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "about": "Committed answers for every new case of the explanation-method pack (TSK-062). Each entry records the signals a grader reads off the answer and the decision the kit must compute from them. test_eval_kit.py checks the decision and ties every form signal (fence, language, image, alt text, markers, block order, asks, bindings, families) to the committed files. A directory answer is laid over the case's fixture: its docs/ files replace or add files and its config.json adds figure bindings and page classes; visual_controls.test.mjs runs the portal adapter on it and applies the explanatory page class rules to the adapted page, and visual_controls_browser.test.mjs renders every declaration it carries. A .json answer is a present document; crates/codeflow-present/tests/method_controls.rs validates it with the present validator. Family, placement, altitude and caption judgments stay the grader's and are recorded, not re-derived. The existing present case in the pack keeps its own controls. A retry entry also lists `judged`, the signals the fixture's judged rubric gives that answer (the evaluator's part of the grade, applied by the builder to these controls), and a faulty entry `caught_by`, the part that fails it: `exact` (anchored/check.py) or `judged` (the rubric). Its `signals` are the checker's output plus `judged`.",
